{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"SUPERPOWERS INLINE-VS-DISPATCHED IS MATERIAL, NOT COSMETIC - quantified today. The superpowers reviewer prompt directs the arm to dispatch a general-purpose subagent. When it cannot, it executes the role in-session and the artifact carries no marker. Previously recorded once (js-gutenberg, refused dispatch under slot pressure). Today both first-attempt runs ALSO ran inline by the arm's own choice, and both re-runs dispatched, giving a direct comparison on the same plans: carbon 12 findings inline versus 13 dispatched, where the subagent caught a FALSE finding of the parent (a claim that cds-icon does not exist, generalised from the first 10 of 470 grep hits) and the parent retracted it; uswds 15 inline versus 20 dispatched, the subagent independently reproducing six findings with matching citations and contributing three the parent had missed. So the dispatched configuration both adds true findings and removes false ones. An inline superpowers run is a different and weaker instrument than a dispatched one, and nothing in its output says which you have."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789443135369761001,"uuid":"2b8b0c90-a027-4888-8238-f712cceebcd0"}